              "exam_name": "NCERT Based",
              "question": "<p>Consider a wire carrying a steady current <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(I,\\)</span> placed in a uniform magnetic field <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(B\\)</span> perpendicular to its length. Consider the charges inside the wire. It is known that magnetic forces do no work. This implies that,</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\"><tbody><tr><td>(a)</td><td>the motion of charges inside the conductor is unaffected by <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(B\\)</span> since they do not absorb energy.</td></tr><tr><td>(b)</td><td>some charges inside the wire move to the surface as a result of <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(B\\)</span>.</td></tr><tr><td>(c)</td><td>if the wire moves under the influence of <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(B\\)</span>, no work is done by the force.</td></tr><tr><td>(d)</td><td>if the wire moves under the influence of <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(B\\)</span>, no work is done by the magnetic force on the ions, assumed fixed within the wire.</td></tr></tbody></table> <p><br>Choose the correct option:<br>1. (b), (c)<br>2. (a), (d)<br>3. (b), (d)<br>4. (c), (d)</p>",
